"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. The surgical findings indicate a high-risk profile with a Gleason 4+5 (ISUP grade group 5) and pT3a stage, with extraprostatic extension present. Favorable findings include negative surgical margins and no invasion of the seminal vesicles, along with no lymph node metastasis documented. The preoperative PSA was 3.7.\n\nCountervailing findings include the absence of documented biopsy grade and ISUP report, which widens uncertainty regarding the true tumor characteristics. The nodal status is documented as negative, which is a positive prognostic factor. The primary uncertainty lies in the missing previous notes, which prevents assessment of postoperative PSA and its trajectory. Information regarding postoperative PSA levels and subsequent changes would significantly revise the prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 39.84 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 29.88–49.80 months; its coverage has not been validated."
